Ported from src/ and the recorded SDK streams in tests/fixtures/sdk-streams/ (MIT,
LICENSE.pi-claude-bridge). Restructured to this repository's extension layout, strict
TypeScript, and lint policy; behavior follows upstream except where listed below.

Source map (upstream src/ → this package):
- index.ts provider stream, consumeQuery, deliverToolResults → stream.ts, query/consume.ts,
  query/events.ts, query/tool-results.ts
- index.ts syncSharedSession, convertAndImportMessages → session/mirror.ts
- index.ts registration, session lifecycle → provider.ts, index.ts, bridge.ts
- index.ts runIsolatedSummary → summary.ts
- index.ts turn/prompt extraction → turn.ts; child env, CLAUDE.md excludes → child.ts
- index.ts tool name/argument mapping, resolveMcpTools → tools.ts
- convert.ts, attachments.ts, session-verify.ts, session-cwd.ts → session/
- prompt-capture.ts, agents-md.ts, skills.ts → prompt/capture.ts; transcript.ts → prompt/
- query-state.ts → query/context.ts; prompt-stream.ts, usage.ts → query/
- models.ts, mcp-server.ts → same names; log-paths.ts → log.ts
- tests/unit-*.mjs → tests/ beside the module each covers (vitest, fake BridgeQuery)
- tests/int-*.{mjs,sh} → tests/turns.integration.test.ts and
  tests/tools.integration.test.ts, skipped unless CLAUDE_BRIDGE_LIVE=1. Not ported:
  int-cc-contracts and int-parallel-tool-results (raw SDK, no pi session), the
  unit-deadlock-log-gate script check, and the end-to-end compaction-owner cases

Deliberate divergences:
- AskClaude tool removed (deprecated upstream in 0.9.3), with its config, UI, and the
  `change-case` dependency; tool names always map to the served MCP names.
- No one-time startup notice and no notice markers written into the config file.
- Debug and diagnostic output is opt-in only (CLAUDE_BRIDGE_DEBUG=1) and lives in
  <agent-dir>/data/claude-bridge/logs/; upstream's unconditional diag log is folded in.
- No config file (config.ts, claude-bridge.json). Its settings are fixed: strict MCP
  config on, auto-memory off, the bundled Claude Code binary, and Opus 4.6 / Sonnet 4.6
  at 200K (no plan, longContextExtraUsage, or forceTwoHundredK).
- rate-limit.ts removed: rate_limit_event is not forwarded to onResponse as
  anthropic-ratelimit-* headers, and allowed_warning utilization notices are dropped.
  A rejection still names the next failure as a non-retryable quota error.
- CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_NONESSENTIAL_TRAFFIC is set on the Claude Code child env instead
  of pi's own process.env.
- The model catalog comes from getBuiltinModels("anthropic") instead of the deprecated
  @earendil-works/pi-ai/compat getModels.
- Process-wide state uses its own global key, so it never shares state with an npm
  pi-claude-bridge install (which would also register the claude-bridge provider:
  uninstall it before loading this one).
- Images with a MIME type the Messages API does not accept are skipped (debug-logged)
  instead of being forwarded and rejected.
- Open stream blocks are tracked in QueryContext.openBlocks instead of temporary
  `index`/`partialJson` fields on pi's content blocks.
- The SDK query is used through the narrower BridgeQuery contract (iteration, interrupt,
  close) so tests inject a fake without module mocking.
- Upstream's "Case N" sync log anchors are kept for log audits and live tests.

